01:03:31.840 --> 01:03:34.400
making whatever, $15 an hour.

1582
01:03:34.400 --> 01:03:36.700
And like, pretending like everything was good.

1583
01:03:37.700 --> 01:03:38.630
That's rough.

1584
01:03:38.630 --> 01:03:40.020
But it was rough before he was able

1585
01:03:40.020 --> 01:03:41.570
to like establish his thing.

1586
01:03:41.570 --> 01:03:43.080
And he started a pest control business,

1587
01:03:43.080 --> 01:03:45.800
'cause that's what he did back east.

1588
01:03:45.800 --> 01:03:48.470
But these kids that I met at church went to my high school

1589
01:03:48.470 --> 01:03:50.820
and it turns out they were all surfers.

1590
01:03:50.820 --> 01:03:53.010
And a couple of them were like, def,

1591
01:03:53.010 --> 01:03:55.310
they weren't like super holy.

1592
01:03:55.310 --> 01:03:56.963
They were like, we're cool.

1593
01:03:57.810 --> 01:03:59.134
And this kid, Justin,

1594
01:03:59.134 --> 01:04:01.416
he invited me to lunch the next day at school.

1595
01:04:01.416 --> 01:04:04.610
And I was so stoked to meet some, some kids that were cool.

1596
01:04:04.610 --> 01:04:06.850
And you could leave campus

1597
01:04:06.850 --> 01:04:07.950
to go, to, to go to lunch,

1598
01:04:07.950 --> 01:04:09.840
which I had never experienced before in the east.

1599
01:04:09.840 --> 01:04:10.990
Like we go to school,

1600
01:04:10.990 --> 01:04:13.940
you're in prison until it's time to get out.

1601
01:04:13.940 --> 01:04:17.100
And we went to this beach parking lot

1602
01:04:17.100 --> 01:04:18.470
after we'd gotten food at a,

1603
01:04:18.470 --> 01:04:21.800
at a place called Carl's Junior that I didn't know existed.

1604
01:04:21.800 --> 01:04:23.980
And we're sitting in the car in the back of his, I mean,

1605
01:04:23.980 --> 01:04:27.140
I'm in the, in the trunk of his Subaru hatchback with,

1606
01:04:27.140 --> 01:04:28.760
in the cars, packed with everybody,

1607
01:04:28.760 --> 01:04:30.150
like, you know, eating

1608
01:04:30.150 --> 01:04:32.588
and they're looking out in the lineup and I look up,

1609
01:04:32.588 --> 01:04:35.823
I'm like, ah, no way.

1610
01:04:37.010 --> 01:04:38.120
Surfing.

1611
01:04:38.120 --> 01:04:40.340
And these guys are speaking in the language,

1612
01:04:40.340 --> 01:04:42.420
talking about what they're seeing waves and swell.

1613
01:04:42.420 --> 01:04:44.020
And I'm just sitting there quiet,

1614
01:04:44.020 --> 01:04:47.420
like what, I'm flashing back to a year ago in Bondai.

1615
01:04:47.420 --> 01:04:50.173
And I was like, hey, I've seen this before.

1616
01:04:51.130 --> 01:04:53.260
And they're like, whatever dude.

1617
01:04:53.260 --> 01:04:54.240
I'm like no,

1618
01:04:54.240 --> 01:04:56.400
I was in Australia last year at Bondai beach.

1619
01:04:56.400 --> 01:04:57.940
And they're like, now what.

1620
01:04:57.940 --> 01:04:59.430
Yeah.

1621
01:04:59.430 --> 01:05:01.513
(laughs)

1622
01:05:02.750 --> 01:05:04.130
Pre-internet, pre,

1623
01:05:04.130 --> 01:05:06.700
like Bondai beach must've been like Oz.

1624
01:05:06.700 --> 01:05:07.533
Yeah.

1625
01:05:07.533 --> 01:05:09.230
I've seen it in magazines and movies.

1626
01:05:09.230 --> 01:05:12.750
And also mind you, there's like couple of--

1627
01:05:12.750 --> 01:05:13.843
Least likely guys never

1628
01:05:13.843 --> 01:05:14.980
they ever imagined.

1629
01:05:14.980 --> 01:05:16.750
There's two other black kids in the school.

1630
01:05:16.750 --> 01:05:18.400
One runs track and the other one

1631
01:05:20.350 --> 01:05:22.420
plays football and I've shown up.

1632
01:05:22.420 --> 01:05:24.220
And they're like, what are you talking about?

1633
01:05:24.220 --> 01:05:25.770
And then I'd tell him my story.

1634
01:05:26.758 --> 01:05:27.880
And like Paul Simon, my dad,

1635
01:05:27.880 --> 01:05:29.130
it's like, who, what?

1636
01:05:29.130 --> 01:05:29.963
Who are you?

1637
01:05:29.963 --> 01:05:31.720
Like, I'm like, I want to do that.

1638
01:05:31.720 --> 01:05:32.900
Like I saw this.

1639
01:05:32.900 --> 01:05:34.980
And I was like, if I ever get a chance,

1640
01:05:34.980 --> 01:05:36.507
I told Justin like, I want to, I want to try it.

1641
01:05:36.507 --> 01:05:37.890
And he's like, all right.

1642
01:05:37.890 --> 01:05:39.240
Be at my house on Saturday.

1643
01:05:40.390 --> 01:05:42.993
And that's how I got to experience surfing.

1644
01:05:43.865 --> 01:05:46.900
We went there and they had a wetsuit and board for me and

1645
01:05:46.900 --> 01:05:47.884
put the wetsuit on backwards.

1646
01:05:47.884 --> 01:05:49.890
Everyone laughed and--
Right.

1647
01:05:49.890 --> 01:05:50.723
I finally made it.

1648
01:05:50.723 --> 01:05:54.061
You ended up surfing like 170 days in a row, right

1649
01:05:54.061 --> 01:05:55.740
without missing a day.

1650
01:05:55.740 --> 01:05:56.573
Yeah.

1651
01:05:56.573 --> 01:05:57.406
I, surfed.

1652
01:05:57.406 --> 01:05:59.320
So there's a, you are committed to figure this out.

1653
01:05:59.320 --> 01:06:02.090
The first time I stood up was like for five seconds.

1654
01:06:02.090 --> 01:06:03.750
And it was literally like,

1655
01:06:03.750 --> 01:06:07.620
I had gone to church thousands of times, you know,

1656
01:06:07.620 --> 01:06:10.750
prayed in groups in large conventions.

1657
01:06:10.750 --> 01:06:13.013
And, and in,

1658
01:06:15.282 --> 01:06:18.480
in know, I, you know, three different religious meetings,

1659
01:06:18.480 --> 01:06:23.480
I never ever felt spirituality before.

1660
01:06:24.420 --> 01:06:27.350
I'd never felt a soul calling

1661
01:06:27.350 --> 01:06:29.710
like I did at 16 and a half,

1662
01:06:29.710 --> 01:06:32.622
standing on a surf board for like five seconds.

1663
01:06:32.622 --> 01:06:34.500
Time stopped,

1664
01:06:34.500 --> 01:06:35.530
everything changed.

1665
01:06:35.530 --> 01:06:37.130
It literally felt like whatever,

1666
01:06:37.130 --> 01:06:38.880
some spirit poured into me.

1667
01:06:38.880 --> 01:06:40.510
And when I came up after falling,

1668
01:06:40.510 --> 01:06:42.770
I screamed as loud as I could.

1669
01:06:42.770 --> 01:06:45.760
And my whole life just pivoted.

1670
01:06:45.760 --> 01:06:48.520
And it was like, okay, this is everything now.

1671
01:06:48.520 --> 01:06:49.983
And I'd never, it was--

1672
01:06:49.983 --> 01:06:51.480
You had that clarity.

1673
01:06:51.480 --> 01:06:52.313
I had that clarity.

1674
01:06:52.313 --> 01:06:54.309
It was the greatest spiritual awakening

1675
01:06:54.309 --> 01:06:57.460
that I could have ever asked for at the time.

1676
01:06:57.460 --> 01:06:59.890
Yeah, I mean, we could talk for

1677
01:06:59.890 --> 01:07:02.170
two hours about the spirituality of surfing,

1678
01:07:02.170 --> 01:07:03.680
but what's interesting is that

1679
01:07:04.930 --> 01:07:07.330
it was etched in your soul in a way

1680
01:07:07.330 --> 01:07:09.350
that almost makes it sound like

1681
01:07:09.350 --> 01:07:10.810
some kind of past life thing.

1682
01:07:10.810 --> 01:07:12.780
Like when you have that experience in Bondai

1683
01:07:12.780 --> 01:07:15.040
and then when you actually connected with it.

1684
01:07:15.040 --> 01:07:16.740
I mean, first of all, you have,

1685
01:07:16.740 --> 01:07:18.280
you have that experience of Bondai

1686
01:07:18.280 --> 01:07:19.650
and there's a knowingness

1687
01:07:19.650 --> 01:07:23.600
about your path on some conscious/unconscious level.

1688
01:07:23.600 --> 01:07:26.970
Then the universe conspires to move you to, you know,

1689
01:07:26.970 --> 01:07:30.230
the epic surf spot in America.

1690
01:07:30.230 --> 01:07:33.470
Like completely, I mean, nobody could have predicted

1691
01:07:33.470 --> 01:07:36.370
a set of circumstances that would bring that about,

1692
01:07:36.370 --> 01:07:40.370
and then the manner in which you just go all in on it

1693
01:07:40.370 --> 01:07:42.823
from the outset, like it's wild.

1694
01:07:44.230 --> 01:07:46.050
In retrospect, yeah.

1695
01:07:46.050 --> 01:07:47.000
You know.
Yeah.

1696
01:07:47.000 --> 01:07:49.180
I mean, it, it just was, it just clicked.

1697
01:07:49.180 --> 01:07:50.960
It was like, oh, this is me,

1698
01:07:50.960 --> 01:07:52.781
everything associated with this.

1699
01:07:52.781 --> 01:07:56.183
I need, I need to just soak.

1700
01:07:57.965 --> 01:07:59.215
I would go to the library

1701
01:08:00.240 --> 01:08:02.690
at school and read back issues of surfer magazine.

1702
01:08:02.690 --> 01:08:07.100
Like I had to learn the culture, the origins, everything.

1703
01:08:07.100 --> 01:08:07.933
And

1704
01:08:09.210 --> 01:08:10.810
as you're coming of age

1705
01:08:10.810 --> 01:08:13.670
and you're dealing with all the challenges

1706
01:08:13.670 --> 01:08:17.530
of your teen angst and then the extra layers of

1707
01:08:17.530 --> 01:08:18.990
that were particular to my family,

1708
01:08:18.990 --> 01:08:20.723
but every kid had a version of it,

1709
01:08:22.140 --> 01:08:25.210
surfing became this mega oasis

1710
01:08:25.210 --> 01:08:26.970
for like none of that mattering,

1711
01:08:26.970 --> 01:08:30.720
like the ultimate freedom of, of expression,

1712
01:08:30.720 --> 01:08:32.473
of like that was the one place

1713
01:08:32.473 --> 01:08:35.190
that I could express myself, wholly

1714
01:08:35.190 --> 01:08:39.550
that I couldn't do with my mom and stepdad.

1715
01:08:39.550 --> 01:08:40.840
And I couldn't even do with my dad.

1716
01:08:40.840 --> 01:08:42.570
Like surfing literally was that place

1717
01:08:42.570 --> 01:08:44.200
where I could just express,

1718
01:08:44.200 --> 01:08:47.640
even though I had the tensions of

1719
01:08:48.800 --> 01:08:51.140
a community that thought they were the definition

1720
01:08:51.140 --> 01:08:51.973
of the thing

1721
01:08:53.040 --> 01:08:55.740
and that they were allowing me to,

1722
01:08:55.740 --> 01:08:58.450
to visit in their space.

1723
01:08:58.450 --> 01:09:02.040
And people, many times feeling uninhibited to tell me

1724
01:09:02.040 --> 01:09:03.210
that I shouldn't be out there

1725
01:09:03.210 --> 01:09:05.603
and using the N word, et cetera, et cetera.

1726
01:09:08.720 --> 01:09:12.470
None of that could actually get in the way of the thing.

1727
01:09:12.470 --> 01:09:14.860
Like when I stood up to do the thing,

1728
01:09:14.860 --> 01:09:16.084
there was no voices except that.

1729
01:09:16.084 --> 01:09:16.917
Wow.

1730
01:09:18.460 --> 01:09:19.760
Point blank.

1731
01:09:19.760 --> 01:09:23.170
Maggie Q is the hero we all need.

1732
01:09:23.170 --> 01:09:24.740
Actress, activist,

1733
01:09:24.740 --> 01:09:27.700
fashion designer, and plant-based icon,

1734
01:09:27.700 --> 01:09:30.830
Maggie is best known for her roles in action films,

1735
01:09:30.830 --> 01:09:34.540
like "Mission Impossible" and the "Divergent" films,

1736
01:09:34.540 --> 01:09:37.410
performing her own stunts on screen

1737
01:09:37.410 --> 01:09:40.840
and advocating for animal rights offscreen.

1738
01:09:40.840 --> 01:09:43.450
In episode 596, Maggie taught us

1739
01:09:43.450 --> 01:09:45.870
the importance of finding your cause

1740
01:09:45.870 --> 01:09:49.520
and giving you're all fighting for it.

1741
01:09:49.520 --> 01:09:52.663
Here's a clip from that empowering exchange.

1742
01:09:54.237 --> 01:09:57.240
I mean, I work, you know, with a group.

1743
01:09:57.240 --> 01:09:58.320
I'm on the board of a group

1744
01:09:58.320 --> 01:10:00.050
called Social Compassion in Legislation.

1745
01:10:00.050 --> 01:10:03.720
We do a lot of legislative work up in Sacramento and,

1746
01:10:03.720 --> 01:10:06.900
you know, it's that it is the epitome of that, right.

1747
01:10:06.900 --> 01:10:08.290
So you sort of like, you know,

1748
01:10:08.290 --> 01:10:11.090
you're going into these meetings with these senators

1749
01:10:11.090 --> 01:10:13.370
and assemblymen and people who can, you know,

1750
01:10:13.370 --> 01:10:15.350
these are lawmakers, these are people that,

1751
01:10:15.350 --> 01:10:18.560
that really essentially work for us, right.

1752
01:10:18.560 --> 01:10:20.310
And you know, I go there and I'm, you know,

1753
01:10:20.310 --> 01:10:23.300
sort of lobbying senators and you know,

1754
01:10:23.300 --> 01:10:24.780
in this building and,

1755
01:10:24.780 --> 01:10:26.520
and then there's no one there.

1756
01:10:26.520 --> 01:10:28.030
And I'm driving down Melrose

1757
01:10:28.030 --> 01:10:32.033
and there's 40 people in line for lip gloss.

1758
01:10:32.033 --> 01:10:34.400
And it, it bums me out because it's like,

1759
01:10:34.400 --> 01:10:35.890
we have so much influence, you know,

1760
01:10:35.890 --> 01:10:37.140
all you have to do is care.

1761
01:10:37.140 --> 01:10:38.070
All you have to do is show up.

1762
01:10:38.070 --> 01:10:39.250
Half of it's showing up, right.

1763
01:10:39.250 --> 01:10:40.480
Life, gotta show up.

1764
01:10:40.480 --> 01:10:42.460
And then once you show up, you know, you,

1765
01:10:42.460 --> 01:10:44.510
you really have to like be in those rooms with people

1766
01:10:44.510 --> 01:10:46.360
that you, that that may not get it.

1767
01:10:46.360 --> 01:10:48.550
But what you're going to do in those rooms

1768
01:10:48.550 --> 01:10:49.719
can be pretty remarkable.

1769
01:10:49.719 --> 01:10:50.552
Yeah.

1770
01:10:50.552 --> 01:10:51.920
Well it's one thing to be

1771
01:10:53.263 --> 01:10:54.880
a proponent of this lifestyle.

1772
01:10:54.880 --> 01:10:57.270
And it's another thing to really shoulder

1773
01:10:57.270 --> 01:11:00.390
that mantle and carry that responsibility to use,

1774
01:11:00.390 --> 01:11:02.800
like the platform that you have to,

1775
01:11:02.800 --> 01:11:04.860
to advocate, you know,

1776
01:11:04.860 --> 01:11:05.960
on behalf of these causes.

1777
01:11:05.960 --> 01:11:08.880
So where does that come from in you?

1778
01:11:08.880 --> 01:11:11.210
Because it would be very easy for you to be like,

1779
01:11:11.210 --> 01:11:12.520
I'm just, I'm doing my movies.

1780
01:11:12.520 --> 01:11:13.760
I don't want to make waves.

1781
01:11:13.760 --> 01:11:15.130
Sure.

1782
01:11:15.130 --> 01:11:16.497
It is much easier to do that.

1783
01:11:16.497 --> 01:11:17.638
Yeah.

1784
01:11:17.638 --> 01:11:18.799
I know, I know it, trust.

1785
01:11:18.799 --> 01:11:20.753
Where does that pull come from?

1786
01:11:22.180 --> 01:11:23.770
I kind of feel like

1787
01:11:27.030 --> 01:11:30.370
it's almost not even a choice in that, you know,

1788
01:11:30.370 --> 01:11:33.200
we live this very privileged existence,

1789
01:11:33.200 --> 01:11:34.760
like in every way, right.

1790
01:11:34.760 --> 01:11:38.240
And I mean that in things that I've earned.

1791
01:11:38.240 --> 01:11:40.040
I mean it, and things that I'm living like, okay,

1792
01:11:40.040 --> 01:11:40.930
I'm given my health,

1793
01:11:40.930 --> 01:11:44.090
I have this gift of health and I can walk and I function.

1794
01:11:44.090 --> 01:11:45.040
So that's a gift.

1795
01:11:45.040 --> 01:11:46.730
And then I've earned these other things

1796
01:11:46.730 --> 01:11:49.310
where I work in Hollywood and I have certain privileges.

1797
01:11:49.310 --> 01:11:51.600
And, and you know, you,

1798
01:11:51.600 --> 01:11:53.950
you start to develop a voice for certain things

1799
01:11:55.120 --> 01:11:56.580
and it doesn't feel like a choice.

1800
01:11:56.580 --> 01:11:58.760
It feels like a responsibility,

1801
01:11:58.760 --> 01:11:59.593
you know, doesn't it,

1802
01:11:59.593 --> 01:12:02.853
when you sort of, when you have a lot, how do you not?

1803
01:12:03.800 --> 01:12:05.370
And it can be anything, you know,

1804
01:12:05.370 --> 01:12:07.610
pick what it is that you sort of feel

1805
01:12:09.550 --> 01:12:12.240
isn't right in your mind, in your heart and your soul.

1806
01:12:12.240 --> 01:12:13.790
And you go out there and you really, you,

1807
01:12:13.790 --> 01:12:14.900
you fight for it.

1808
01:12:14.900 --> 01:12:16.640
And you hope that other people will do the same

1809
01:12:16.640 --> 01:12:17.760
when something matters to them,

1810
01:12:17.760 --> 01:12:19.050
because I'm sure you get this all the time.

1811
01:12:19.050 --> 01:12:20.440
I've gotten it for 20 years.

1812
01:12:20.440 --> 01:12:21.700
Like, oh, you don't care about kids.

1813
01:12:21.700 --> 01:12:22.810
You don't care about women.

1814
01:12:22.810 --> 01:12:25.680
You don't care about, you know, libraries.

1815
01:12:25.680 --> 01:12:26.513
I don't know.

1816
01:12:26.513 --> 01:12:28.327
Because you've chosen to advocate for one thing.

1817
01:12:28.327 --> 01:12:32.163
That's at the exclusion of other things that are important.

1818
01:12:32.163 --> 01:12:33.386
That's exactly it.

1819
01:12:33.386 --> 01:12:34.219
I'm like, you're so right.

1820
01:12:34.219 --> 01:12:36.850
I hate children because I love the environment

1821
01:12:36.850 --> 01:12:38.010
or whatever it is, you know.

1822
01:12:38.010 --> 01:12:39.740
And it sort of is there's always this line.

1823
01:12:39.740 --> 01:12:42.517
And so it's always this thing of like, you know,

1824
01:12:42.517 --> 01:12:44.240
I have people that write into me and go,

1825
01:12:44.240 --> 01:12:45.900
you care more about homeless pets

1826
01:12:45.900 --> 01:12:47.410
than you do about homeless children.

1827
01:12:47.410 --> 01:12:48.810
I'm like interesting.

1828
01:12:48.810 --> 01:12:49.643
And I said,

1829
01:12:49.643 --> 01:12:52.640
I'm so glad that you care about homeless children.

1830
01:12:52.640 --> 01:12:53.610
Well, I do.

1831
01:12:53.610 --> 01:12:54.684
I said, well, tell me more.

1832
01:12:54.684 --> 01:12:56.530
What do you, what do you do for homeless children?

1833
01:12:56.530 --> 01:12:57.363
I'm fascinated.

1834
01:12:57.363 --> 01:12:58.196
I want to know.

1835
01:12:59.170 --> 01:13:00.050
Nothing.
Crickets.

1836
01:13:00.050 --> 01:13:01.730
Absolutely nothing.

1837
01:13:01.730 --> 01:13:03.811
So I've never ever run into a person

1838
01:13:03.811 --> 01:13:05.520
who puts themselves out there,

