and truly ever wanted to know about,

2886
01:50:44.450 --> 01:50:46.630
you guessed it, sleep.

2887
01:50:46.630 --> 01:50:49.240
All in all, this is life altering listening

2888
01:50:49.240 --> 01:50:52.800
that will completely reshape your relationship with slumber.

2889
01:50:52.800 --> 01:50:55.743
Here's a powerful clip from episode 600.

2890
01:50:57.340 --> 01:50:59.813
Sleep really is right up there with outer space

2891
01:50:59.813 --> 01:51:02.924
and the depths of the ocean in terms of its,

2892
01:51:02.924 --> 01:51:05.220
its mysteries, and you know, the,

2893
01:51:05.220 --> 01:51:07.210
the idea that we're just beginning to learn

2894
01:51:07.210 --> 01:51:08.540
what's actually going on.

2895
01:51:08.540 --> 01:51:10.530
And it's not a matter of,

2896
01:51:10.530 --> 01:51:11.900
I'm sure you get this question all the time.

2897
01:51:11.900 --> 01:51:13.560
Like, well, what's more important REM sleep

2898
01:51:13.560 --> 01:51:15.287
or non-REM sleep, or what,

2899
01:51:15.287 --> 01:51:17.744
you know, what's the, you know,

2900
01:51:17.744 --> 01:51:19.695
the sort of significance of being deprived

2901
01:51:19.695 --> 01:51:21.280
of one over the other,

2902
01:51:21.280 --> 01:51:23.740
but it's really the interplay of all of these things.

2903
01:51:23.740 --> 01:51:26.460
And the more complex you realize it to be,

2904
01:51:26.460 --> 01:51:29.220
it becomes impossible to consider

2905
01:51:29.220 --> 01:51:32.730
that it's not crucial to all facets of human health.

2906
01:51:32.730 --> 01:51:33.563
That's right.

2907
01:51:33.563 --> 01:51:34.530
And, you know, when we go back

2908
01:51:34.530 --> 01:51:38.040
to that evolutionary story of, of how,

2909
01:51:38.040 --> 01:51:41.250
you know, detrimental sleep is as a state, and it is.

2910
01:51:41.250 --> 01:51:42.930
Let's face it.

2911
01:51:42.930 --> 01:51:45.500
You know, if there were any stage of sleep

2912
01:51:45.500 --> 01:51:47.040
that were not important,

2913
01:51:47.040 --> 01:51:50.000
that mother nature could have come in and excised

2914
01:51:50.000 --> 01:51:51.220
and had you, you know,

2915
01:51:51.220 --> 01:51:54.060
doing all of these benefits of wakefulness (mumbles).

2916
01:51:54.060 --> 01:51:56.520
I'm quite sure she would have.

2917
01:51:56.520 --> 01:51:57.630
And what we've learned

2918
01:51:57.630 --> 01:52:00.460
is that every stage of sleep is important.

2919
01:52:00.460 --> 01:52:01.910
Different stages of sleep

2920
01:52:01.910 --> 01:52:04.810
perform different functions for the brain and body

2921
01:52:04.810 --> 01:52:07.022
at different times of night.

2922
01:52:07.022 --> 01:52:09.530
And so, yeah, I often get that question.

2923
01:52:09.530 --> 01:52:11.500
People will say, how can I get more deep sleep,

2924
01:52:11.500 --> 01:52:14.210
or how can I get more REM sleep?

2925
01:52:14.210 --> 01:52:15.940
And, you know, I often say, well,

2926
01:52:15.940 --> 01:52:17.760
why do you want more of that?

2927
01:52:17.760 --> 01:52:19.900
And they say, well, isn't that the good stuff?

2928
01:52:19.900 --> 01:52:23.170
And they're both absolutely critical.

2929
01:52:23.170 --> 01:52:27.260
Now I could make a scientific argument

2930
01:52:27.260 --> 01:52:30.290
that REM sleep could be a little bit more important

2931
01:52:30.290 --> 01:52:33.270
from a simple mortality state,

2932
01:52:33.270 --> 01:52:36.250
because there were studies done back in the 1980s with rats,

2933
01:52:36.250 --> 01:52:39.367
and they've actually never been replicated again.

2934
01:52:39.367 --> 01:52:41.280
Now I found them difficult to read.

2935
01:52:41.280 --> 01:52:43.230
I do research in humans.

2936
01:52:43.230 --> 01:52:45.441
I don't do animal research.

2937
01:52:45.441 --> 01:52:48.760
And I think they won't be replicated for good reason.

2938
01:52:48.760 --> 01:52:52.100
What they wanted to do is see if a lack of sleep

2939
01:52:52.100 --> 01:52:54.930
is deathly, is a lack of sleep fatal.

2940
01:52:54.930 --> 01:52:58.240
And they had three different flavors of the experiment.

2941
01:52:58.240 --> 01:52:59.720
In the first, they took rats

2942
01:52:59.720 --> 01:53:01.810
and they just deprive them of sleep,

2943
01:53:01.810 --> 01:53:03.300
you know, night and day after day,

2944
01:53:03.300 --> 01:53:04.660
night and day after day.

2945
01:53:04.660 --> 01:53:07.080
And what they found is that those rats died

2946
01:53:07.080 --> 01:53:09.310
within about 20 days.

2947
01:53:09.310 --> 01:53:10.870
So in other words,

2948
01:53:10.870 --> 01:53:15.140
rats will die as quickly from a lack of food

2949
01:53:15.140 --> 01:53:16.950
as they will from a lack of sleep.

2950
01:53:16.950 --> 01:53:20.040
That's how fundamental it is.

2951
01:53:20.040 --> 01:53:22.830
Then the two additional flavors of the experiment,

2952
01:53:22.830 --> 01:53:24.910
they selectively deprive them

2953
01:53:24.910 --> 01:53:27.200
of either just rapid eye movement sleep

2954
01:53:27.200 --> 01:53:29.400
so that they could get just non-REM

2955
01:53:29.400 --> 01:53:30.600
or they did the opposite.

2956
01:53:30.600 --> 01:53:33.403
They just deprived them of non-REM and gave them REM.

2957
01:53:34.450 --> 01:53:36.500
And firstly, both of those were fatal.

2958
01:53:36.500 --> 01:53:38.790
But what was interesting is that

2959
01:53:38.790 --> 01:53:41.330
the rats died from REM sleep deprivation

2960
01:53:41.330 --> 01:53:44.150
within about 30 to 40 days.

2961
01:53:44.150 --> 01:53:47.080
And they died from deep non-REM sleep deprivation

2962
01:53:47.080 --> 01:53:49.840
within about 50 or 60 days.

2963
01:53:49.840 --> 01:53:53.130
So if we want to sort of do a Coke Pepsi challenge

2964
01:53:53.130 --> 01:53:56.130
between sort of, you know, non-REM and REM,

2965
01:53:56.130 --> 01:53:58.970
which one wins out in the mortality battle,

2966
01:53:58.970 --> 01:54:01.143
it seems to be REM sleep.

2967
01:54:01.143 --> 01:54:03.300
And, and to me, that's interesting too.

2968
01:54:03.300 --> 01:54:06.900
I, if you'd asked me where I would place my bets,

2969
01:54:06.900 --> 01:54:08.420
I would've said non-REM.

2970
01:54:08.420 --> 01:54:11.570
The reason is because non-REM came first.

2971
01:54:11.570 --> 01:54:14.070
If you look during the sort of the time course

2972
01:54:14.070 --> 01:54:16.973
of evolution of across phylogeny,

2973
01:54:17.930 --> 01:54:21.020
non-REM sleep was the first sleep to emerge.

2974
01:54:21.020 --> 01:54:22.990
And it was only when we went

2975
01:54:22.990 --> 01:54:25.490
from reptiles, amphibians and fish.

2976
01:54:25.490 --> 01:54:27.410
And then there was that bifurcation

2977
01:54:27.410 --> 01:54:29.630
to birds and then mammals

2978
01:54:29.630 --> 01:54:32.340
did the evolution of REM sleep emerge.

2979
01:54:32.340 --> 01:54:35.460
So REM sleep is the new kid on the evolutionary block.

2980
01:54:35.460 --> 01:54:39.125
And furthermore, REM sleep evolved twice independently

2981
01:54:39.125 --> 01:54:41.600
in birds and mammals,

2982
01:54:41.600 --> 01:54:43.310
which I find is fascinating too.

2983
01:54:43.310 --> 01:54:47.501
So to come back to your point, I'm sorry, I'm drifting,

2984
01:54:47.501 --> 01:54:49.904
but all stages of sleep are critical.

2985
01:54:49.904 --> 01:54:52.710
No one stage of sleep you can do without,

2986
01:54:52.710 --> 01:54:54.290
without suffering detriment.

2987
01:54:54.290 --> 01:54:55.123
Right.

2988
01:54:55.123 --> 01:54:57.980
I think if I were to have something, a single sentence,

2989
01:54:57.980 --> 01:55:01.600
I would say that sleep is the single most effective thing

2990
01:55:01.600 --> 01:55:03.320
that we can do each day

2991
01:55:03.320 --> 01:55:06.313
to reset the health of our brain and our body.

2992
01:55:07.700 --> 01:55:10.010
That would be a beautiful place to end this,

2993
01:55:10.010 --> 01:55:11.820
but I just realized there's an important thing

2994
01:55:11.820 --> 01:55:13.050
we also didn't talk about

2995
01:55:13.050 --> 01:55:14.730
that I would like you to touch on quickly.

2996
01:55:14.730 --> 01:55:15.563
Yeah, of course.

2997
01:55:15.563 --> 01:55:16.688
Which is the, the,

2998
01:55:16.688 --> 01:55:17.521
you talked at the,

2999
01:55:17.521 --> 01:55:20.350
at the outset about

3000
01:55:20.350 --> 01:55:22.100
what happens when you get a flu shot

3001
01:55:22.100 --> 01:55:23.680
and you're sleep deprived.

3002
01:55:23.680 --> 01:55:25.860
We're still in the midst of this pandemic.

3003
01:55:25.860 --> 01:55:27.370
We're slowly emerging out of it,

3004
01:55:27.370 --> 01:55:28.690
but can you talk a little bit

3005
01:55:28.690 --> 01:55:30.240
about what you've learned about

3006
01:55:31.270 --> 01:55:32.667
sleep, COVID,

3007
01:55:34.120 --> 01:55:39.040
immunity and how people should be kind of thinking about

3008
01:55:39.040 --> 01:55:42.680
how their relationship with, with the virus?

3009
01:55:42.680 --> 01:55:44.630
Yeah, so let me,

3010
01:55:44.630 --> 01:55:47.390
I'll speak about sleep and immunity sort of more generally,

3011
01:55:47.390 --> 01:55:48.870
and then come on to sleep COVID

3012
01:55:48.870 --> 01:55:52.040
because sleep has changed in at least four different ways

3013
01:55:52.040 --> 01:55:53.270
because of COVID,

3014
01:55:53.270 --> 01:55:57.794
quantity, quality, timing, and dreaming.

3015
01:55:57.794 --> 01:56:00.560
So I'll try to mentally put those stickies

3016
01:56:00.560 --> 01:56:03.233
up on my cerebral wall so I come back to them.

3017
01:56:04.215 --> 01:56:06.030
But in terms of sleep and immunity,

3018
01:56:06.030 --> 01:56:08.440
there is a very intimate association

3019
01:56:08.440 --> 01:56:11.170
between your sleep health and your immune health.

3020
01:56:11.170 --> 01:56:12.980
Firstly, what we know is that individuals

3021
01:56:12.980 --> 01:56:16.573
who report sleeping less than seven hours a night

3022
01:56:16.573 --> 01:56:20.610
are almost three times more likely to become infected

3023
01:56:20.610 --> 01:56:23.670
by the rhino virus, which is the common cold.

3024
01:56:23.670 --> 01:56:26.180
Second we know from a prospective study in,

3025
01:56:26.180 --> 01:56:28.570
I think it was well over 30,000 women,

3026
01:56:28.570 --> 01:56:31.670
women sleeping five hours or less a night

3027
01:56:31.670 --> 01:56:36.240
are more than 60% more likely to develop pneumonia

3028
01:56:36.240 --> 01:56:37.980
across a five-year period,

3029
01:56:37.980 --> 01:56:39.720
which of course is a critical part

3030
01:56:39.720 --> 01:56:42.500
of the COVID mortality equation.

3031
01:56:42.500 --> 01:56:44.680
We've also mentioned that statistic about

3032
01:56:44.680 --> 01:56:47.020
if you're not getting sleep in the week before

3033
01:56:47.020 --> 01:56:47.900
you get your flu shot,

3034
01:56:47.900 --> 01:56:50.410
you can't produce the normal antibody response.

3035
01:56:50.410 --> 01:56:53.480
Do we know that that's the case for COVID yet?

3036
01:56:53.480 --> 01:56:54.313
No we don't.

3037
01:56:54.313 --> 01:56:55.360
But we're looking at that.

3038
01:56:55.360 --> 01:56:57.114
We also know it's the case for Hepatitis A,

3039
01:56:57.114 --> 01:56:59.460
Hepatitis B vaccination too.

3040
01:56:59.460 --> 01:57:01.660
So I think there's an interesting case to be made

3041
01:57:01.660 --> 01:57:03.260
that it could make a difference.

3042
01:57:05.220 --> 01:57:08.430
We also know that just as we mentioned before,

3043
01:57:08.430 --> 01:57:09.920
just one night of short sleep,

3044
01:57:09.920 --> 01:57:10.930
you know, just four hours,

3045
01:57:10.930 --> 01:57:13.430
we'll drop those critical anti-cancer fighting cells,

3046
01:57:13.430 --> 01:57:17.270
natural killer cells by 70%.

3047
01:57:17.270 --> 01:57:19.590
If that's true, then why,

3048
01:57:19.590 --> 01:57:22.990
what is sleep doing for our emotional health

3049
01:57:22.990 --> 01:57:26.280
and sleep provides us with that sort of sorry,

3050
01:57:26.280 --> 01:57:27.956
not emotional health, for our immune health.

3051
01:57:27.956 --> 01:57:30.930
It provides us two different benefits.

3052
01:57:30.930 --> 01:57:32.460
Firstly, it's during sleep,

3053
01:57:32.460 --> 01:57:34.230
and particularly during deep sleep,

3054
01:57:34.230 --> 01:57:37.970
where the body will be stimulated to produce

3055
01:57:37.970 --> 01:57:40.663
many more of those critical immune factors.

3056
01:57:41.540 --> 01:57:45.410
Even better, the sleep will actually increase

3057
01:57:45.410 --> 01:57:49.710
the sensitivity and the receptivity of your body

3058
01:57:49.710 --> 01:57:52.653
to those increased immune factors.

3059
01:57:53.530 --> 01:57:56.340
So you wake up the next morning

3060
01:57:56.340 --> 01:57:59.630
as a more robust immune individual.

3061
01:57:59.630 --> 01:58:04.383
Sleep will restock the weaponry in your immune arsenal.

3062
01:58:05.750 --> 01:58:07.930
So on that basis,

3063
01:58:07.930 --> 01:58:11.403
I think sleep has become very relevant in this pandemic.

